@@ -70,6 +70,18 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object with ``str()``, joins them with ``sep`` and writes them followed by ``end``. Here's an example::
+
+    console.out("Hello", "World", sep=", ", style="bold")
+
+``out`` does not pretty print containers, wrap or crop text, interpret console markup, or replace emoji codes. Text is written literally. It does apply highlighting by default, and it accepts a basic ``style``. Pass ``highlight=False`` to turn highlighting off for a call, or ``highlight=None`` to use the console's setting.
+
+Internally, ``out`` delegates to :meth:`~rich.console.Console.print`, so render hooks and capturing work as they do for print.
+
+
